// FIRST DRAFT (phase 6): rewrite or sign off. Voice: docs/voice.md. Flags: docs/story-drafts.md.
// The seeress's first night (docs/tech-spec.md §72): you carried old Heid's staff from farm to farm, and she sleeps by your mother's fire now.
Folded inside Ulf's letter is a second scrap, in a hand you'd know anywhere: Heid's runes, small and very straight, as if they'd run off if she let them.
"I saw you with a stamp in your hand three winters back. I didn't tell you. You'd only have asked what it was for." # speaker: heid
"Your mother has given me the warm corner. Asa brings my porridge and asks whether she'll marry a king. I tell her the porridge is too thick to read." # speaker: heid
"Ask me one thing, girl. I'll answer it true. It's all I've got left to give." # speaker: heid
* ["How does it end?"]
  # fx: flag heid_asked_end
  "Badly for most. Well for a few. Odin asked me the same once, at my door, in a hat pulled down over his eye. He didn't like the answer either." # speaker: heid
* ["Will they be all right?"]
  # fx: flag heid_asked_home
  "That depends on you. Which is why I'm writing to you, and not to them." # speaker: heid
- You keep her scrap under your cot. In the morning Ulf's letter has gone with the raven, and hers is still there. She'll have known it would be.
-> END
